          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 233.37,
          "end": 236.1,
          "en": "because answer text is now a variable,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 236.1,
          "end": 239.01,
          "en": "actually one that doesn't change, but still,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 239.01,
          "end": 241.53,
          "en": "the text widget can no longer be used",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 241.53,
          "end": 244.23,
          "en": "in conjunction with the const keyword here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 244.23,
          "end": 246.18,
          "en": "That's not all I want to accept here though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 246.18,
          "end": 247.77,
          "en": "Instead this function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 247.77,
          "end": 251.52,
          "en": "which is set as a value for on pressed on the button,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 251.52,
          "end": 253.83,
          "en": "should also be coming from outside.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 253.83,
          "end": 257.58,
          "en": "So it should also be settable from inside questions screen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 257.58,
          "end": 260.82,
          "en": "so that we can then in the end pass our answer text",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 260.82,
          "end": 263.94,
          "en": "to this answer widget, and then as a second argument,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 263.94,
          "end": 266.97,
          "en": "also our function that should be executed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 266.97,
          "end": 269.193,
          "en": "when the button is pressed, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 270.45,
          "end": 273.65999999999997,
          "en": "And to achieve this, we must accept another argument,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 273.65999999999997,
          "end": 277.08,
          "en": "a positional or named argument, that is up to you,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 277.08,
          "end": 279.42,
          "en": "as part of this answer button.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 279.42,
          "end": 281.67,
          "en": "And for that I'll add another property here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 281.67,
          "end": 284.35,
          "en": "which should be of type function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 285.33,
          "end": 288.57,
          "en": "that actually returns no value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 288.57,
          "end": 292.17,
          "en": "So I want to get a function that returns no value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 292.17,
          "end": 295.23,
          "en": "and I'll name this one here onTap.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 295.23,
          "end": 297.48,
          "en": "The name is up to you though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 297.48,
          "end": 301.35,
          "en": "And accept another argument, which is also named onTap,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 301.35,
          "end": 303.21,
          "en": "and which is then automatically used",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 303.21,
          "end": 305.1,
          "en": "as a value for this property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 305.1,
          "end": 307.443,
          "en": "by adding this dot in front of it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 308.79,
          "end": 311.61,
          "en": "And then it's this onTap variable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 311.61,
          "end": 315.3,
          "en": "that can be used as a value for on pressed here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 315.3,
          "end": 318.57,
          "en": "On tapped is the function which we receive as an argument,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 318.57,
          "end": 320.43,
          "en": "and which we then use as a value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 320.43,
          "end": 323.58,
          "en": "for on pressed on the elevated button, and therefore,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 323.58,
          "end": 326.91,
          "en": "we'll be able to pass a function here to the answer widget",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 326.91,
          "end": 328.86,
          "en": "when we use it in another widget,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 328.86,
          "end": 331.17,
          "en": "like here in questions screen,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 331.17,
          "end": 333.06,
          "en": "so that we can define which function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 333.06,
          "end": 336,
          "en": "should in the end be executed when this button is pressed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 336,
          "end": 337.26,
          "en": "from inside the widget",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 337.26,
          "end": 340.23,
          "en": "where we use our custom answer widget.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 340.23,
          "end": 343.29,
          "en": "And of course, all these positional arguments here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 343.29,
          "end": 346.05,
          "en": "could also be set up as named arguments.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 346.05,
          "end": 349.32,
          "en": "And just to also show you how this would work,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 349.32,
          "end": 353.76,
          "en": "I'll actually convert these positional two named arguments,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 353.76,
          "end": 355.11,
          "en": "not because you have to,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 355.11,
          "end": 356.64,
          "en": "but because it can be interesting",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 356.64,
          "end": 358.56,
          "en": "to see how this could be done.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 358.56,
          "end": 362.22,
          "en": "You simply place these arguments between these curly braces",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 362.22,
          "end": 364.68,
          "en": "in your argument list here then,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 364.68,
          "end": 367.32,
          "en": "and now you must add required,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 367.32,
          "end": 370.62,
          "en": "the extra required keyword in front of them,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 370.62,
          "end": 375.06,
          "en": "because by default in Dart, named arguments are optional,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 375.06,
          "end": 376.83,
          "en": "but here we need values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 376.83,
          "end": 380.22,
          "en": "to make sure that this answer button widget works correctly,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 380.22,
          "end": 382.86,
          "en": "and therefore, we must make them non-optional",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 382.86,
          "end": 384.78,
          "en": "by adding the required keyword",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 384.78,
          "end": 386.853,
          "en": "in front of the named arguments.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 387.99,
          "end": 391.14,
          "en": "Besides that, they now work like positional arguments.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 391.14,
          "end": 392.88,
          "en": "They can receive values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 392.88,
          "end": 395.37,
          "en": "and these values are then forwarded",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 395.37,
          "end": 397.05,
          "en": "thanks to the this keyword",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 397.05,
          "end": 399.99,
          "en": "to the properties that have the same names.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 399.99,
          "end": 402.983,
          "en": "So answer text to answer text and onTap to onTap.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
